## DML.cls review (v4.1.0)

Sorted by priority, then effort. Easy = a few lines and one test. Medium = several classes or a design decision. Lines = saved per copy; every change goes into both DML.cls copies.

### Bugs

| Status | # | Priority | Effort | Bug | Fix |
|--------|---|----------|--------|-----|-----|
| [x] | 1 | High | Easy | A record pointing at the same parent twice (e.g. `Asset.AccountId` + `AssetServicedById`) failed with "Cyclic dependencies detected among records." | Count each parent once in `addDependency` (dfbf154) |
| [x] | 2 | High | Easy | `*Immediately` ignored `withSharing()`/`withoutSharing()` in `systemMode()` (broken since v3.0.0) | `executeImmediately` goes through `commitWork` and the sharing executor (b05dccc) |
| [ ] | 3 | High | Easy | `dryRun()` then `commitWork()` on the same instance throws "Duplicate records found during registration." (`DependencyOrchestrator` keeps its map and graph) | Create the two fields at the top of `DependencyOrchestrator.execute()` |
| [ ] | 4 | High | Medium | After `dryRun()` or a failed `commitTransaction()`, records keep rolled-back Ids, so committing them fails with "Only records without an Id can be registered as new."; examples.md "Validating Before Committing" always fails | Clear Ids of records that had none after the rollback (both orchestrator paths), never after a failed `commitWork()`; update the two `selfDependency` asserts. Stopgap: fix the docs example |
| [ ] | 5 | Medium | Easy | Operations outlive commits: same Error ID / `operationId()` across commits on one instance (e.g. `DML.Shared`); a later `toMerge` with the same master Id merges the first master record | Create the operation storage in `reset()` |
| [x] | 6 | Medium | Easy | `retrieveResultFor(id)` went stale after the first read (`successes()`, `failures()`, `errors()`, `hasFailures()`) | Fill the lists as results are added, no cache (c057668) |
| [ ] | 7 | Medium | Easy | In an org with a top-level `DML.Logger`, it replaces the injected test logger; `loggerOnFailedDml`, `loggerOnPartialSuccess`, `loggerOnFailedChunk` fail in subscriber orgs | `dmlLogger` setter also sets `isLoggerInitialized = true` |
| [ ] | 8 | Low | Easy | `DML.Records(...).withRelationship(field, externalIdField, value)` describes 2 fields per record on every commit | Describe once in the `ExternalRelationship` constructor |
| [ ] | 9 | Low | Easy | `new DML(null)` throws a NullPointerException | Clear `DmlException` or default order; decide with 17 |
| [ ] | 10 | Low | Easy | `chunkSize(0)` runs an extra empty chunk; a negative value turns chunking off | Leave, or treat values below 1 like `null` |

